From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:51:28 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: offer HDMI 3D modes only on HDMI signals

The HDMI 1.4a 3D structures are signalled by the HDMI vendor InfoFrame
(HDMI 1.4a, section 8.2.3), which
fill_stream_properties_from_drm_display_mode() sends only when the stream
signal is HDMI. Since stereo was allowed on every connector, the 3D modes
of a sink's HDMI VSDB were listed whatever the signal:
- a DisplayPort sink with an HDMI VSDB in its EDID got HDMI 3D modes it
  was never told about, and frame packing even got its doubled timing on
  the DisplayPort link (create_stream_for_sink());
- the HDMI sink behind a DP-to-HDMI protocol converter got the same
  unsignalled modes, as no InfoFrame SDP carries the vendor InfoFrame;
- a sink DC drives in DVI mode (through a DP++ adaptor on a board
  without HDMI audio on dongles, or a DVI connector) takes no InfoFrame
  at all.
Only sinks on a signal other than HDMI are affected; a passive DP++
adaptor in HDMI mode makes the sink signal HDMI (DC's
decide_signal_from_strap_and_dongle_type()), and its 3D modes stay.

Refuse the HDMI 3D layouts, every stereo layout but frame sequential, when
the sink signal is not HDMI: amdgpu_dm_connector_mode_valid() returns
MODE_NO_STEREO, so the modes are no longer listed, and
amdgpu_dm_create_validate_stream_for_sink() builds no stream, so an atomic
commit of such a mode fails too. Frame sequential is DisplayPort's own
stereo and is refused by the DRM core until amdgpu opts in.

Nothing a sink could show is lost: those modes never switched it into 3D,
and its 2D modes are unchanged. The protocol converter case comes back
once the vendor InfoFrame is sent in an InfoFrame SDP.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c   | 26 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.h   |  1 +
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
index b0dcedad8..91ddd315d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -2322,6 +2322,25 @@ dm_validate_stream_color_format(const struct drm_connector_state *drm_state,
 		DC_OK : DC_UNSUPPORTED_VALUE;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The HDMI 1.4a 3D structures are signalled by the HDMI vendor InfoFrame
+ * (section 8.2.3), which fill_stream_properties_from_drm_display_mode() sends
+ * only on an HDMI stream: an HDMI connector, a DP++ adaptor in HDMI mode, or a
+ * DVI connector driving an HDMI sink. On any other signal the sink would get
+ * the 3D timing with nothing to tell it: a DVI sink takes no InfoFrame, and no
+ * InfoFrame reaches a DisplayPort sink, or the HDMI sink behind a DP-to-HDMI
+ * protocol converter, as none is sent in an InfoFrame SDP yet.
+ */
+STATIC_IFN_KUNIT bool dm_sink_signals_hdmi_3d(const struct dc_sink *sink)
+{
+	return sink && dc_is_hdmi_signal(sink->sink_signal);
+}
+
+static bool dm_mode_is_hdmi_3d(const struct drm_display_mode *mode)
+{
+	return drm_mode_is_stereo(mode) && !drm_mode_is_frame_sequential(mode);
+}
+
 struct dc_stream_state *
 amdgpu_dm_create_validate_stream_for_sink(struct drm_connector *connector,
 					  const struct drm_display_mode *drm_mode,
@@ -2376,6 +2395,10 @@ amdgpu_dm_create_validate_stream_for_sink(struct drm_connector *connector,
 		return stream;
 	}
 
+	if (dm_mode_is_hdmi_3d(drm_mode) &&
+	    !dm_sink_signals_hdmi_3d(aconnector->dc_sink))
+		return NULL;
+
 	signal = aconnector->dc_link->connector_signal;
 
 	/*
@@ -2572,6 +2595,9 @@ enum drm_mode_status amdgpu_dm_connector_mode_valid(struct drm_connector *connec
 		goto fail;
 	}
 
+	if (dm_mode_is_hdmi_3d(mode) && !dm_sink_signals_hdmi_3d(dc_sink))
+		return MODE_NO_STEREO;
+
 	test_mode = drm_mode_duplicate(connector->dev, mode);
 	if (!test_mode)
 		goto fail;
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.h
index 4e9eb3ff2..566478501 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.h
@@ -179,6 +179,7 @@ int dm_encoder_helper_atomic_check(struct drm_encoder *encoder,
 				   struct drm_crtc_state *crtc_state,
 				   struct drm_connector_state *conn_state);
 enum drm_mode_subconnector get_subconnector_type(struct dc_link *link);
+bool dm_sink_signals_hdmi_3d(const struct dc_sink *sink);
 void update_subconnector_property(struct amdgpu_dm_connector *aconnector);
 void amdgpu_dm_fbc_init(struct drm_connector *connector);
 void amdgpu_dm_set_panel_type(struct amdgpu_dm_connector *aconnector);
-- 
